(* ::Package:: *)

(* ::Title:: *)
(*Equation checks for "Gravitational collapse in Lorentz-violating gravity and the spin-0 mode"*)


(* ::Text:: *)
(*PURPOSE.  An independent Wolfram Language audit of the paper (main.tex): every displayed or labelled equation,*)
(*every inline relation and every piece of arithmetic.  The 4d geometry of the code's metric, the aether stress*)
(*tensor and the constraints are derived from first principles and the paper's statements are compared with the*)
(*derivation.  The simulation numbers quoted in the paper are collected in one association (DATA, section 0b)*)
(*with their main.tex line and verbatim snippet; the arithmetic-consistency sections read from it.*)
(**)
(*WHAT IS NOT CHECKED.  Raw simulation output (measured convergence orders, horizon radii, energies, white-hole*)
(*times and widths) and literature inputs (the sign of the spin-0 mode energy, the GW170817 bound, the field*)
(*equations of Taherasghari and Will) are not re-derived: the sections that quote them report SKIP, and the DATA*)
(*sections only test the paper's own arithmetic on those numbers.  The three mode speeds of eq:speeds are derived*)
(*from the action (S06).*)
(**)
(*REQUIREMENTS AND USAGE.  Mathematica 14.2 (wolframscript).*)
(*    wolframscript -file check_equations.wl [path/to/main.tex]*)
(*(or  math -script check_equations.wl,  or  Get["check_equations.wl"]  in a kernel).  main.tex is used only by the*)
(*snippet cross-check (the last section, S81): its path is the first command-line argument, else the environment*)
(*variable PAPER_TEX, else "main.tex" in the current directory; if the file is absent that section reports SKIP and*)
(*everything else runs unchanged.  Run time about 40 s, most of it the geometry setup of section 0a and the*)
(*plane-wave derivation S06.  Exit code (as a script): 1 if any section FAILs, else 0 (CAVEATs do not change it).*)
(*The notebook check_equations.nb contains the same code (one Input cell per section, generated by make_notebook.wl);*)
(*evaluate it top to bottom.  README_mathematica.md has a run log and the equation list.*)
(**)
(*STATUS LINES.  Each section prints exactly one line  PASS / FAIL / CAVEAT / SKIP  with a residual; a summary table*)
(*and the counts are printed at the end.  PASS = the statement is derived or verified;  FAIL = the statement as*)
(*written in main.tex is wrong;  CAVEAT = the statement is correct only with a qualification, or a printed detail*)
(*(a number, a factor, a wording) does not match what the paper's own equations or numbers give -- the section*)
(*comment and the status line say what; it is a finding for the authors, not a failure of the script (exit code*)
(*unchanged);  SKIP = simulation data or literature input, not checkable from equations (or, for S81, main.tex not*)
(*found).*)
(**)
(*DATA AND THE SNIPPET CHECK.  Each DATA entry is  key -> <|"v" -> value, "L" -> "main.tex line(s)", "tex" ->*)
(*"snippet as printed"|>; the checks read dat["key"] and datL["key"], so a changed number is updated in one place.*)
(*S81 verifies that every snippet occurs on its quoted line(s) of main.tex (whitespace, backslashes, braces, $ and ~*)
(*ignored): this guards every section that reads DATA, and the wording of every claim entry (the quoted relations and*)
(*sentences, "v" -> Null, and the claim numbers dmClaim, coulombClaim, q2Claim; README_mathematica.md lists which*)
(*section tests or quotes each).  Measured values that the paper does NOT print are kept apart, in RECORD (section 0b).*)
(**)
(*CONVENTIONS.  Signature (-,+,+,+); u.u = -1; ds^2 = -N^2 dt^2 + (dr + beta dt)^2 + Theta^2 dOmega^2 (gamma_rr = 1);*)
(*u_a = -N d_a t; K_ab = -h_a^c nabla_c u_b, trK = -nabla_a u^a, Q = K^r_r - trK/3; a_a = u^b nabla_b u_a;*)
(*field equations G_ab = T_ab (the normalisation of the code and of eq:lum; derived in S33/S59); aether stress*)
(*tensor from arXiv:1501.07274 eq. (2.34).*)
(**)
(*TRANSCRIBED, NOT DERIVED.  The evolution equations of P, trK, a_r and Theta (codeRHS), the Hamiltonian constraint*)
(*diagnostic (thetaCcode), the momentum-constraint ODE (momConCode), the coefficients aN, bN, the outer-boundary*)
(*treatment, the initial-data profile and the ALE taper are transcribed from the simulation code release/collapse.cpp*)
(*of this repository.  Code lines are written collapse.cpp:L..., never bare L... (= main.tex):*)
(*header equations collapse.cpp:L44-76; compute_RHS collapse.cpp:L817-930, interior loop L844-890, outer boundary*)
(*L892-929; theta_C collapse.cpp:L1305-1315; compute_Q collapse.cpp:L699-735; couplings and spin0_aN/bN in main*)
(*collapse.cpp:L1607-1616; set_initial_data collapse.cpp:L1208-1298, ingoing P L1252-1261; quintic_taper*)
(*collapse.cpp:L325-332.  This script does NOT derive those equations from the action: the SymPy audit*)
(*(check_equations.py, its S04/S10) does.  What IS derived here from first principles: the 4d geometry of the metric*)
(*(Christoffels, Einstein tensor, nabla u, a_a, K_ab), the Misner-Sharp identities, the aether stress tensor and the*)
(*two constraints (S59, which shows that the transcribed theta_C and compute_Q are G_uu = T_uu and G_ue = T_ue), the*)
(*constraint propagation (S16), the linearisation, the asymptotic solution, the boundary-condition algebra, the*)
(*matrix algebra of the post-Newtonian argument and the normalisation kappa = 1.  The principal-part sections (S36-S41)*)
(*check that the PAPER matches the transcribed CODE.*)
(**)
(*PAPER SOURCE VERSION.  Line numbers and the DATA snippets refer to main.tex of the paper's LaTeX source (arXiv v1).*)
(*Against another version of the source, S81 lists the entries whose snippet or line has moved.*)


(* ::Section:: *)
(*0a. Setup: bookkeeping, couplings, code equations, geometry (no checks here)*)


ClearAll["Global`*"];
$HistoryLength = 0;
results = {};
residString[e_] := If[ByteCount[e] > 3000, "<large expression>", ToString[e, InputForm]];
report[id_String, line_String, what_String, ok_, resid_] := Module[{tag},
  tag = Which[ok === True, "PASS", ok === False, "FAIL", ok === "CAVEAT", "CAVEAT", True, "SKIP"];
  AppendTo[results, {id, line, tag, what, residString[resid]}];
  Print[tag, ": ", id, " [", If[StringStartsQ[line, "collapse.cpp"], line, "main.tex L" <> line], "] ", what, "   | residual: ", residString[resid]];
];
isZero[e_] := Module[{s}, s = Quiet[Simplify[Together[e]]]; TrueQ[s === 0]];
isZeroAll[l_] := And @@ (isZero /@ Flatten[{l}]);
close[x_, y_, tol_] := TrueQ[Abs[x - y] <= tol];
closeAll[x_List, y_List, tol_] := Length[x] == Length[y] && And @@ MapThread[close[#1, #2, tol] &, {x, y}];
halvingQ[l_List, tol_] := And @@ (close[#, 2, tol] & /@ Ratios[1/l]);   (* a factor-2 grid ladder *)

(* coupling combinations, kept symbolic in c1..c4 *)
c13 = c1 + c3; c14 = c1 + c4; c123 = c1 + c2 + c3;
den = 2 + c13 + 3 c2;
den1 = c14 (1 - c13);
aN = (c14 - 2)/den;              (* main.tex eq:aNbN, collapse.cpp:L1615 spin0_aN *)
bN = -c123/den1;                 (* main.tex eq:aNbN, collapse.cpp:L1616 spin0_bN *)
v2sq = 1/(1 - c13);
v1sq = (2 c1 - c1^2 + c3^2)/(2 c14 (1 - c13));
v0sq = c123 (2 - c14)/(c14 (1 - c13) (2 + c13 + 3 c2));
couplBase = {c1 -> 7/10, c2 -> -5119403/10000000, c3 -> 0, c4 -> 0};   (* main.tex L477 *)
couplC20 = {c1 -> 7/10, c2 -> 0, c3 -> 0, c4 -> 0};                     (* main.tex L479 *)

(* The equations evolved by collapse.cpp (compute_RHS, interior loop collapse.cpp:L844-890), for arbitrary field expressions of (t,r).
   Order: {Theta, psi, P, trK, a_r}.  Shift beta enters as  d_t f = beta f' + N(...). *)
codeRHS[lapE_, shE_, thE_, psE_, mE_, kE_, qE_, aE_] := {
  shE D[thE, r] + lapE thE (qE/2 - kE/3),
  shE D[psE, r] + lapE mE,
  shE D[mE, r] + lapE (kE mE + aE D[psE, r] + D[psE, {r, 2}] + 2 D[thE, r] D[psE, r]/thE),
  shE D[kE, r] + lapE kE^2/3 + lapE ((c14 - 2) (D[aE, r] + 2 D[thE, r] aE/thE + aE^2) + 2 mE^2 + 3 (1 - c13) qE^2)/den,
  shE D[aE, r] + lapE ((2 kE/3 - qE) aE + (c13/den1) mE D[psE, r] - (c123/den1) D[kE, r])};
(* collapse.cpp theta_C() (collapse.cpp:L1305-1315):  Theta times the Hamiltonian constraint C *)
thetaCcode[thE_, psE_, mE_, kE_, qE_, aE_] := thE D[thE, {r, 2}] + (D[thE, r]^2 - 1)/2 + c14 aE thE D[thE, r] +
  (thE^2/4) (c14 (2 D[aE, r] + aE^2) + mE^2 + D[psE, r]^2 + (3/2) (1 - c13) qE^2 - (1/3) den kE^2);
(* collapse.cpp compute_Q() (collapse.cpp:L699-735):  Q' = -3 Q Theta'/Theta + (-P psi' + den/3 trK')/(1-c13), written as M = 0 *)
momConCode[thE_, psE_, mE_, kE_, qE_] := (den/3) D[kE, r] - (1 - c13) (D[qE, r] + 3 qE D[thE, r]/thE) - mE D[psE, r];

(* Field names used throughout (the paper's symbols; collapse.cpp names in brackets):
     Nf = lapse N [NN],  betaf = shift beta [NR],  Thf = areal radius Theta [Theta],  psi = scalar psi [Psi],
     Pf = scalar momentum P = u(psi) [P],  trk = trK [trK],  Qf = shear Q [Q],  arf = aether acceleration a_r [Acr].
   ThfDot, psiDot, PfDot, trkDot, arfDot are their code time derivatives at fixed r. *)
fields = {Nf[t, r], betaf[t, r], Thf[t, r], psi[t, r], Pf[t, r], trk[t, r], Qf[t, r], arf[t, r]};
{ThfDot, psiDot, PfDot, trkDot, arfDot} = codeRHS @@ fields;

(* Reduction rules.  kinRules use only DEFINITIONS (gauge gamma_rr=1, a_r = d_r ln N, d_t Theta from K and Q,
   P = u.grad psi).  evoRules add the code's evolution equations for trK, a_r, P. *)
kinRules = {
  Derivative[m_, n_][betaf][t, r] /; n >= 1 :> D[Nf[t, r] (Qf[t, r] + trk[t, r]/3), {t, m}, {r, n - 1}],
  Derivative[m_, n_][Nf][t, r] /; n >= 1 :> D[arf[t, r] Nf[t, r], {t, m}, {r, n - 1}],
  Derivative[m_, n_][Thf][t, r] /; m >= 1 :> D[ThfDot, {t, m - 1}, {r, n}],
  Derivative[m_, n_][psi][t, r] /; m >= 1 :> D[psiDot, {t, m - 1}, {r, n}]};
evoRules = Join[kinRules, {
  Derivative[m_, n_][trk][t, r] /; m >= 1 :> D[trkDot, {t, m - 1}, {r, n}],
  Derivative[m_, n_][arf][t, r] /; m >= 1 :> D[arfDot, {t, m - 1}, {r, n}],
  Derivative[m_, n_][Pf][t, r] /; m >= 1 :> D[PfDot, {t, m - 1}, {r, n}]}];
kinReduce[e_] := Simplify[Together[e //. kinRules]];
evoReduce[e_] := Simplify[Together[e //. evoRules]];
timeDerivs[e_] := Union[Cases[e, Derivative[m_, _][f_][t, r] /; m >= 1 :> f, Infinity]];

(* ---- 4d geometry of the code's metric ---- *)
X = {t, r, thA, phA};
gmet = {{-Nf[t, r]^2 + betaf[t, r]^2, betaf[t, r], 0, 0}, {betaf[t, r], 1, 0, 0}, {0, 0, Thf[t, r]^2, 0}, {0, 0, 0, Thf[t, r]^2 Sin[thA]^2}};
ginv = Simplify[Inverse[gmet]];
Gam = Table[Simplify[(1/2) Sum[ginv[[a, d]] (D[gmet[[d, b]], X[[c]]] + D[gmet[[d, c]], X[[b]]] - D[gmet[[b, c]], X[[d]]]), {d, 4}]], {a, 4}, {b, 4}, {c, 4}];  (* Gam[[a,b,c]] = Gamma^a_bc *)
Ric = Table[Simplify[Sum[D[Gam[[m, a, b]], X[[m]]] - D[Gam[[m, a, m]], X[[b]]], {m, 4}] +
     Sum[Gam[[m, m, l]] Gam[[l, a, b]] - Gam[[m, b, l]] Gam[[l, a, m]], {m, 4}, {l, 4}]], {a, 4}, {b, 4}];
Rsc = Simplify[Sum[ginv[[a, b]] Ric[[a, b]], {a, 4}, {b, 4}]];
Ein = Simplify[Ric - Rsc gmet/2];      (* G_ab *)
EinMD = Simplify[Ein . ginv];          (* G_a^b *)
uLo = {-Nf[t, r], 0, 0, 0};           (* u_a = -N grad_a t *)
uUp = Simplify[ginv . uLo];
eUp = {0, 1, 0, 0}; eLo = gmet . eUp;  (* unit radial vector (gamma_rr = 1) *)
Dl = Simplify[Table[D[uLo[[b]], X[[a]]] - Sum[Gam[[c, a, b]] uLo[[c]], {c, 4}], {a, 4}, {b, 4}]];  (* nabla_a u_b *)
Du = Simplify[Table[Sum[ginv[[b, c]] Dl[[a, c]], {c, 4}], {a, 4}, {b, 4}]];                     (* nabla_a u^b *)
divu = Simplify[Sum[Du[[a, a]], {a, 4}]];
accLo = Simplify[Table[Sum[uUp[[b]] Dl[[b, a]], {b, 4}], {a, 4}]];                               (* a_a = u^b nabla_b u_a *)
accUp = Simplify[ginv . accLo];
Kab = Simplify[Table[-Sum[(KroneckerDelta[a, c] + uLo[[a]] uUp[[c]]) Dl[[c, b]], {c, 4}], {a, 4}, {b, 4}]];
KrrM = Simplify[Kab[[2, 2]]]; KththM = Simplify[Kab[[3, 3]]/Thf[t, r]^2];
trKM = KrrM + 2 KththM; QM = KrrM - trKM/3;
dTh = Table[D[Thf[t, r], X[[a]]], {a, 4}];
hMS = Simplify[dTh . ginv . dTh];                      (* (grad Theta)^2 *)
mMS = Thf[t, r] (1 - hMS)/2;                            (* Misner-Sharp mass *)
AA = Simplify[uUp . dTh]; BB = D[Thf[t, r], r];         (* A = u.grad Theta, B = d_r Theta *)
rhoG = Simplify[uUp . Ein . uUp]; jG = Simplify[-uUp . Ein . eUp]; pG = Simplify[eUp . Ein . eUp];
Print["setup done, ", ToString[NumberForm[SessionTime[], {Infinity, 1}]], " s"];



