(*36. Eq. evolution as a first-order system (L755-761): trK, a_r lines = code; block-triangular principal symbol*)


(* LaTeX (L755-761): "With $\partial_r\psi$ as an extra variable, Eqs.~\eqref{eq:evolution} are first order in time and
   space ... The equations for $\psi$, $P$ and $\Theta$ contain no derivatives of $\trK$ or $a_r$, so the principal symbol is
   block-triangular and the spin-0 speeds are those of the $(\trK,a_r)$ block".
   Check: (i) the trK and a_r lines of eq:evolution (L348-353), written as d_t f = beta f' + N[...] and typed in
