   psi rather than d_r psi as the variable the psi' column is N P times a constant (c13 P psi' in the a_r equation), and these
   are the only two non-zero entries.  In the wave zone a_r ~ P ~ 1/r (neither vanishes) and Theta = r, so the two couplings
   fall off as r^-2 and r^-1 while the principal entries stay O(1); P = psi' = 0 alone leaves the Theta coupling.
   The (phi, P) block is [[beta, N], [N, beta]]: P - phi belongs to beta - N (rdot = -beta + N, outgoing) and P + phi to
   beta + N (ingoing); the eigenvalues of S are beta +- N v0 and beta +- N, beta (Theta): the speeds are unchanged. *)
Block[{vars, dvars, sub, rhs, phiRHS, S, lout, lin, colTh, colPsi, kTh, kPsi, wz},
  sub = {Derivative[0, 1][trk][t, r] -> dK, Derivative[0, 1][arf][t, r] -> dA, Derivative[0, 1][Thf][t, r] -> dT,
     Derivative[0, 2][psi][t, r] -> dF, Derivative[0, 1][psi][t, r] -> phi, Derivative[0, 1][Pf][t, r] -> dP};
  rhs = (codeRHS @@ fields) /. sub;
  phiRHS = betaf[t, r] dF + Nf[t, r] dP;          (* principal part of d_r(beta phi + N P) *)
  S = Table[D[{rhs[[4]], rhs[[5]], rhs[[1]], phiRHS, rhs[[3]]}[[i]], {dK, dA, dT, dF, dP}[[j]]], {i, 5}, {j, 5}];
  lout = {-bN/Sqrt[v0sq], 1, 0, 0, 0}; lin = {bN/Sqrt[v0sq], 1, 0, 0, 0};
  res41 = Simplify[{lout . S - (betaf[t, r] - Nf[t, r] Sqrt[v0sq]) lout, lin . S - (betaf[t, r] + Nf[t, r] Sqrt[v0sq]) lin}];
  res41b = Simplify[{res41 /. arf[t, r] -> 0, {-1, 1} . {{betaf[t, r], Nf[t, r]}, {Nf[t, r], betaf[t, r]}} - (betaf[t, r] - Nf[t, r]) {-1, 1},
      {1, 1} . {{betaf[t, r], Nf[t, r]}, {Nf[t, r], betaf[t, r]}} - (betaf[t, r] + Nf[t, r]) {1, 1}, S[[4 ;; 5, 4 ;; 5]] - {{betaf[t, r], Nf[t, r]}, {Nf[t, r], betaf[t, r]}}}];
  colTh = Simplify[res41[[1, 3]]];
  colPsi = Simplify[lout[[1 ;; 2]] . {D[rhs[[4]], phi], D[rhs[[5]], phi]}];     (* psi' column with psi as the variable *)
  kTh = Simplify[colTh Thf[t, r]/(Nf[t, r] arf[t, r])]; kPsi = Simplify[colPsi/(Nf[t, r] Pf[t, r])];
  wz = {Thf[t, r] -> rw41, arf[t, r] -> al41/rw41, Pf[t, r] -> pp41/rw41, Nf[t, r] -> 1};
  ok41 = isZeroAll[res41b] && ! isZero[colTh] && ! isZero[colPsi] &&
    FreeQ[kTh, t | r] && FreeQ[kPsi, t | r] && isZeroAll[{res41[[1, {1, 2, 4, 5}]], res41[[2, {1, 2, 4, 5}]]}] &&
    Limit[colTh /. wz, rw41 -> Infinity] === 0 && Limit[colPsi /. wz, rw41 -> Infinity] === 0 &&
    FreeQ[Simplify[rw41^2 colTh /. wz], rw41] && FreeQ[Simplify[rw41 colPsi /. wz], rw41] &&
    ! isZero[colTh /. {Pf[t, r] -> 0, phi -> 0}];
report["S41 exact char. variables", "799-804", "padded w_out, w_in: only a Theta' entry N a_r/Theta x " <> ToString[NumberForm[N[kTh /. couplBase], 4]] <>
  " and a psi' entry N P x " <> ToString[NumberForm[N[kPsi /. couplBase], 4]] <> "; ~ r^-2, r^-1 for a_r ~ P ~ 1/r (neither zero): exact far out; P -+ psi' <-> beta -+ N",
  ok41, {res41, kTh, kPsi}];
];


(* ::Section:: *)
(*42. Linearised system far from the source (inline, L809-823)*)


(* LaTeX (L810-818): "We solve them in the static frame of flat space, $N=1$ and zero shift, with the areal radius $\Theta=r$ as
   radial coordinate. " + DATA "rigidShift" (L812-818); (L818-823) "Keeping only the terms linear in the fields, the $\trK$ and $a_r$ equations of Eq.~\eqref{eq:evolution} become
   $\partial_t\trK=a_N\,r^{-2}\partial_r(r^2a_r)$ and $\partial_t a_r=b_N\,\partial_r\trK$; the scalar drops out, since it enters
   them only quadratically".
   Check (derivation): linearise the code's trK and a_r equations about N=1, beta=0, Theta=r, all other fields zero
   (fields scaled by eps, first order).  Perturbations of N, beta, Theta multiply background sources that vanish, so they
   drop out at this order; the scalar enters only quadratically (decouples).  Translation: -dt^2 + dR^2 with R = r + c(t) is
   -dt^2 + (dr + c' dt)^2 (N = 1, gamma_rr = 1, beta = c'); beta = -1 gives c = -t + const, so a point at fixed r has
   dR/dt = -1 (falls inward at unit speed); d_t|_R = d_t|_r - c' d_r = d_t - beta d_r ("a time derivative at fixed areal
   radius becomes d_t - beta d_r").  NOTE: this is the flat-space statement; on the collapse background
   d_t|_Theta = d_t - (beta + N A/B) d_r (A = u(Theta), B = Theta'), which the paper approximates "with the time derivative at
   fixed areal radius divided by the lapse and Theta for r" (L864-866). *)
Block[{lin, cc = cfn[t], g1, g2, w, csol},
  g1 = Expand[-dt^2 + (D[r + cc, t] dt + dr)^2]; g2 = Expand[-dt^2 + (dr + D[cc, t] dt)^2];
  w = HH[r + cc, t];
  csol = cfn[t] /. First[DSolve[cfn'[t] == dat["rigidShift"], cfn[t], t]];
  tr42 = Simplify[{g1 - g2, D[w, t] - D[cc, t] D[w, r] - (Derivative[0, 1][HH][r + cc, t]), D[r + csol, t] + 1, D[csol, t, t]}];
  lin = D[codeRHS[1, 0, r, eps psi[t, r], eps Pf[t, r], eps trk[t, r], eps Qf[t, r], eps arf[t, r]], eps] /. eps -> 0;
  res42 = Simplify[{lin[[4]] - aN/r^2 D[r^2 arf[t, r], r], lin[[5]] - bN D[trk[t, r], r]}];
];
report["S42 linearised system", datL["rigidShift"] <> ",809-823", "static frame and the rigid translation r -> r + c(t) (beta = c', gamma_rr = 1; beta = -1 => c = -t + const, dR/dt = -1; d_t|_R = d_t - beta d_r, flat space); linearised code equations", isZeroAll[res42] && isZeroAll[tr42], {res42, tr42}];


(* ::Section:: *)
(*43. Wave equation (L823-824)*)


(* LaTeX (L823-824): "Together they give the wave equation $\partial_t^2\trK=v_0^2\,r^{-2}\partial_r(r^2\partial_r\trK)$".
   Check: d_t of the first linearised equation, with d_t a_r = bN trK', gives aN bN = v0^2 times the spherical Laplacian. *)
res43 = Simplify[(aN/r^2 D[r^2 (bN D[trk[t, r], r]), r]) - v0sq/r^2 D[r^2 D[trk[t, r], r], r]];
report["S43 wave equation", "823-824", "d_t^2 trK = v0^2 Laplacian trK", res43 === 0, res43];


(* ::Section:: *)
(*44. eq:asymptotic (L824-834)*)


(* LaTeX (L828-830): \trK=\frac{f(u)}{r},\qquad a_r=-\frac{b_N}{v_0}\,\frac{f(u)}{r}-b_N\,\frac{F(u)}{r^2},\\ u=t-\frac{r}{v_0},\quad F'=f;
   (L834) "where the profile $f$ is set by the source and $F$ is its integral".
   Check: exact solution of the linearised system and of the wave equation for arbitrary F (aN = v0^2/bN). *)
Block[{u, kS, aS},
  u = t - r/v; kS = FF'[u]/r; aS = -bb2/v FF'[u]/r - bb2 FF[u]/r^2;
  res44 = Simplify[{D[kS, t] - (v^2/bb2)/r^2 D[r^2 aS, r], D[aS, t] - bb2 D[kS, r], D[kS, {t, 2}] - v^2/r^2 D[r^2 D[kS, r], r]}];
];
report["S44 eq:asymptotic", "824-834", "outgoing solution solves the linearised system and the wave equation exactly", isZeroAll[res44], res44];


(* ::Section:: *)
(*45. eq:wout-asym (L835-847): the 1/r^2 part, the waveform, w_in changes while the pulse goes by*)


(* LaTeX (L835-836): "Besides the $1/r$ falloff of any spherical wave, $a_r$ has a $1/r^2$ part, which builds up as the pulse goes by and
   remains behind it"; (L839-841): \wout=-\frac{2b_N}{v_0}\,\frac{f(u)}{r}-b_N\,\frac{F(u)}{r^2},\qquad \win=-b_N\,\frac{F(u)}{r^2};
   (L844-846) "The radiation is carried by $\wout$, and $r\,\wout\to-2b_Nf(u)/v_0$ is the spin-0 waveform we extract. The ingoing
   variable $\win$ has no $1/r$ part, but it is not zero: it changes while the pulse goes by".
   Check (derivation): substitute eq:asymptotic into eq:wout; lim r w_out = -2 bN f/v0; w_in has no 1/r part and
   d_t w_in = -bN trK/r (F' = f); the O(1/r) part (f/r)(1, -bN/v0) is parallel to the right eigenvector (-aN/v0, 1) of lambda_-
   (supporting algebra); for a positive pulse on |u| < 1, F = Int f grows during the pulse and is constant after it. *)
Block[{u, kS, aS, Ms, e, lead, fp45, F45},
  u = t - r/v; kS = FF'[u]/r; aS = -bb2/v FF'[u]/r - bb2 FF[u]/r^2;
  Ms = {{bb, nn aa}, {nn bb2, bb}}; e = {-aa/v, 1};
  lead = {1, -bb2/v};          (* coefficient of f(u)/r in (trK, a_r) *)
  res45 = Simplify[{(-bb2/v kS + aS) - (-2 bb2/v FF'[u]/r - bb2 FF[u]/r^2), (bb2/v kS + aS) - (-bb2 FF[u]/r^2),
      ((-aa/v) lead - e) /. aa -> v^2/bb2, (Ms . e - (bb - nn v) e) /. aa -> v^2/bb2,
      D[bb2/v kS + aS, t] + bb2 kS/r, Limit[r (-2 bb2/v ff0/r - bb2 FF0/r^2), r -> Infinity] + 2 bb2 ff0/v}];
  fp45[x_?NumericQ] := If[Abs[x] < 1, Exp[-1/(1 - x^2)], 0];
  F45 = Table[NIntegrate[fp45[x], {x, -1, Min[uu, 1]}], {uu, {-0.5, 0., 0.5, 1.5, 2., 5.}}];
report["S45 eq:wout-asym, waveform, d_t w_in", "835-847", "r w_out -> -2 bN f/v0; w_in has no 1/r part, d_t w_in = -bN trK/r (changes while the pulse goes by); the 1/r^2 part F grows during the pulse and stays after it", isZeroAll[res45] && Less @@ F45[[1 ;; 4]] && Max[F45[[4 ;;]]] - Min[F45[[4 ;;]]] < 10^-8, {res45, F45}];
];


(* ::Section:: *)
(*46. eq:retarded (L911-921, in the Extraction paragraph)*)


(* LaTeX (L911-914): "To compare spheres we use the retarded time" u=t-\frac{\Theta_*}{v_0},\qquad
   \Theta_*=\Theta+2\MADM\ln\!\left(\frac{\Theta}{2\MADM}-1\right); (L917-919) "the flat-space $u$ of Eq.~\eqref{eq:asymptotic} with $r$
   replaced by the Schwarzschild tortoise coordinate $\Theta_*$, which accounts approximately for the slowing of the wave near
   the black hole"; (L920-921) "The narrow pulse drifts slowly in $u$ (Fig.~\ref{fig:wout}(b)), which we attribute to this approximation".
   Check: dTheta_*/dTheta = 1/(1-2M/Theta) (Schwarzschild tortoise); along u = const, dTheta/dt = v0 (1 - 2M/Theta) < v0 (slowing).
   Fig. 3 caption writes u = t - Theta_*: the same for v0 = 1. *)
Block[{Th, MM}, res46 = Simplify[{D[Th + 2 MM Log[Th/(2 MM) - 1], Th] - 1/(1 - 2 MM/Th), v/D[Th + 2 MM Log[Th/(2 MM) - 1], Th] - v (1 - 2 MM/Th)}];];
report["S46 eq:retarded", "911-921,931", "Schwarzschild tortoise derivative; dTheta/dt = v0(1 - 2M/Theta) along u = const (slowing near the black hole)", isZeroAll[res46], res46];


(* ::Section:: *)
(*47. Inline (L849-850): parities at r = 0 are preserved by the evolution equations*)


(* LaTeX (L849-850): "At $r=0$ we impose regularity: $\psi$, $P$, $\trK$ and $Q$ are even in $r$, and $\Theta$, $a_r$ and
   $\beta$ are odd".
   Check (derivation): with Taylor series of these parities (and the lapse even, since d_r ln N = a_r is odd), the
   transcribed right-hand sides of Theta, psi, P, trK, a_r have the same parity as the field: the coefficients of the wrong
   parity vanish up to r^5.  Also beta = Int_0^r N(Q + trK/3) of an even integrand is odd, and the regular Q from the
   momentum constraint is even (Q = q2 r^2 + ..., S16). *)
Block[{thS, psS, momS, kS, aS, qS, lapS, shS, rhs, wrong},
  thS = r + t3 r^3 + t5 r^5; psS = s0 + s2 r^2 + s4 r^4; momS = m0 + m2 r^2 + m4 r^4; kS = k0 + k2 r^2 + k4 r^4;
  aS = e1 r + e3 r^3 + e5 r^5; qS = g2 r^2 + g4 r^4; lapS = n0 + n2 r^2 + n4 r^4; shS = b1 r + b3 r^3 + b5 r^5;
  rhs = codeRHS[lapS, shS, thS, psS, momS, kS, qS, aS];
  wrong = {Table[SeriesCoefficient[rhs[[1]], {r, 0, j}], {j, {0, 2, 4}}], Table[SeriesCoefficient[rhs[[2]], {r, 0, j}], {j, {1, 3, 5}}],
     Table[SeriesCoefficient[rhs[[3]], {r, 0, j}], {j, {1, 3}}], Table[SeriesCoefficient[rhs[[4]], {r, 0, j}], {j, {1, 3}}],
     Table[SeriesCoefficient[rhs[[5]], {r, 0, j}], {j, {0, 2, 4}}],
     Table[SeriesCoefficient[Integrate[(lapS (qS + kS/3)) /. r -> x, {x, 0, r}], {r, 0, j}], {j, {0, 2, 4}}]};
  res47 = Simplify[wrong];
];
report["S47 parities at r=0", "849-850", "RHS of the odd fields (Theta, a_r) odd and of the even fields (psi, P, trK) even; beta odd", isZeroAll[res47], res47];


(* ::Section:: *)
(*48. Outer boundary (L851-853): entering fields w_in and P + d_r psi; the code update (projector algebra, code check)*)


(* LaTeX (L851-853): "At the outer boundary a condition is needed only for the fields that enter the grid there, $\win$ for the
   spin-0 pair and $P+\partial_r\psi$ for the scalar; the outgoing fields simply leave."  The projector form of the
   condition is not printed; its algebra is kept as a check of the code update.
   Check (derivation, general aN, bN with v0 = sqrt(aN bN)): e+- = (+-aN/v0, 1) and theta^+- = (+-bN/v0, 1) are right/left
   eigenvectors of M for beta +- N v0; theta^-.e+ = theta^+.e- = 0 and theta+.e+ = 2, so the normalised entering pair is
   (theta+, e+/2); at r_max only lambda_+ can be positive while lambda_- < 0 (theta+.u = w_in enters, rdot = -beta - N v0 < 0);
   P = I - (e+/2) theta+ obeys P^2 = P, P e+ = 0, theta+ P = 0, theta- P = theta-; with R = M d_r u + S generic,
   theta+.(P R + (e+/2) B) = B and theta-.(P R + (e+/2) B) = theta-.R; the code's update equals P R + (e+/2) G, i.e. the
   paper's condition with B = G, and is independent of the normalisation of the pair (e -> e/s, theta -> s theta). *)
Block[{Ms, vv, ep, em, tp, tm, Pm, R, code, ein, sS, G, R1, R2},
  vv = Sqrt[aNs bNs];
  Ms = {{bt, nn aNs}, {nn bNs, bt}};
  ep = {aNs/vv, 1}; em = {-aNs/vv, 1}; tp = {bNs/vv, 1}; tm = {-bNs/vv, 1};
  ein = ep/2; Pm = IdentityMatrix[2] - Outer[Times, ein, tp];
  R = {R1, R2};
  code = R - ep (tp . R - G)/(tp . ep);
  res48 = Simplify[{Ms . ep - (bt + nn vv) ep, Ms . em - (bt - nn vv) em, tp . Ms - (bt + nn vv) tp, tm . Ms - (bt - nn vv) tm,
      tm . ep, tp . em, tp . ep - 2, Pm . Pm - Pm, Pm . ep, tp . Pm, tm . Pm - tm,
      tp . (Pm . R + ein G) - G, tm . (Pm . R + ein G) - tm . R, code - (Pm . R + ein G),
      (IdentityMatrix[2] - Outer[Times, ein/sS, sS tp]) - Pm}, aNs > 0 && bNs > 0];
];
report["S48 entering fields; code update", datL["outgoingUnchanged"], "w_in = theta+.u is the field with lambda_+ (enters iff lambda_+ > 0); code check: eigenpairs, theta^J.e_I = delta (theta+.e+ = 2 in the code), P^2 = P, P e_in = 0, theta^in P = 0, theta^out P = theta^out; d_t(theta^in.u) = B; code update = P R + e_in G", isZeroAll[res48], res48];


(* ::Section:: *)
(*49. eq:bc-win (L853-870): entering fields of an outgoing wave; r trK constant along the outgoing characteristics <=> d_t w_in = -b_N trK/r; (d_t - beta d_r) w_in = -N b_N trK/Theta*)


(* LaTeX: DATA "noIncoming" (L853-860), "outgoingChar" (L860-864); (L864-866) "on the collapse background, with the time
   derivative at fixed areal radius divided by the lapse and $\Theta$ for $r$, it reads" (L868)
   (\partial_t-\beta\partial_r)\win=-Nb_N\,\frac{\trK}{\Theta}.
   Check (derivation): (i) w_in = -bN F/r^2 -> 0 at infinity for bounded F, one power of r below w_out (ratio v0 F/(2 f r));
   (ii) for the linear system d_t K = aN r^-2 d_r(r^2 a), d_t a = bN d_r K with aN bN = v0^2, the identity
   d_t w_in + bN K/r = (bN/(v0 r)) (d_t + v0 d_r)(r K) holds for ANY K, a, so (bN != 0) "r trK = f(u) constant along the
   outgoing characteristics of speed v0" is equivalent to d_t w_in = -bN trK/r; (iii) N^-1(d_t - beta d_r) = u.grad;
   (iv) flat space in the code's gauge with CONSTANT lapse N and shift beta: T = N t, R = r + beta t brings
   -N^2 dt^2 + (dr + beta dt)^2 to -dT^2 + dR^2, the aether is at rest in (T, R) and Theta = R.  The outgoing solution of
   S44 written in (T, R), trK = f(T - R/v0)/R, a_r = -(bN/v0) f/R - bN F/R^2, solves the linearised code equations in (t, r)
   with this N, beta (d_t = beta d_r + N(...)), and for it (d_t - beta d_r) w_in = N d_T w_in = -N bN trK/Theta EXACTLY;
   hence d_t w_in = beta d_r w_in - N bN trK/Theta, which is the code's G (B = G = d_t w_in of the outgoing wave). *)
Block[{Kl, al, dtK, dta},
  Kl = kk49[t, r]; al = aa49[t, r];
  dtK = (v^2/bb2) D[r^2 al, r]/r^2; dta = bb2 D[Kl, r];
  equiv49 = Simplify[(bb2/v dtK + dta + bb2 Kl/r) - bb2/(v r) (r dtK + v D[r Kl, r])];
];
Block[{TT, RR, kS, aS, win, eqK, eqA},
  TT = nl t; RR = r + bs t;
  kS = FF'[TT - RR/v]/RR; aS = -bb2/v FF'[TT - RR/v]/RR - bb2 FF[TT - RR/v]/RR^2;
  eqK = D[kS, t] - (bs D[kS, r] + nl (v^2/bb2) (D[aS, r] + 2 D[RR, r] aS/RR));       (* linearised code trK eq., aN = v^2/bN *)
  eqA = D[aS, t] - (bs D[aS, r] + nl bb2 D[kS, r]);
  win = bb2/v kS + aS;
  res49 = Simplify[{eqK, eqA, D[RR, t] - (bs D[RR, r]), (D[win, t] - bs D[win, r]) + nl bb2 kS/RR, D[win, t] - (bs D[win, r] - nl bb2 kS/RR),
     Limit[-bb2 ArcTan[t - r/v]/r^2, r -> Infinity, Assumptions -> v > 0] (* bounded F: w_in -> 0 *),
     uUp . {D[wfun[t, r], t], D[wfun[t, r], r], 0, 0} - (D[wfun[t, r], t] - betaf[t, r] D[wfun[t, r], r])/Nf[t, r],
     ((bb2 FF[t - r/v]/r^2)/(2 bb2/v FF'[t - r/v]/r)) r - v FF[t - r/v]/(2 FF'[t - r/v])}];
];
report["S49 eq:bc-win", datL["noIncoming"] <> "," <> datL["outgoingChar"] <> "," <> datL["binRate"] <> ",collapse.cpp:L911", "w_in = -bN F/r^2 -> 0 at infinity, |w_in|/|w_out| = v0 F/(2 f r) (one power of r below); linear system: d_t w_in + bN K/r = (bN/(v0 r))(d_t + v0 d_r)(r K) identically (equivalence); N^-1(d_t - beta d_r) = u.grad; flat space, constant N, beta: eq:bc-win exact for the outgoing wave; code G = beta d_r w_in - N bN K/Theta = d_t w_in", isZeroAll[res49] && isZero[equiv49], {res49, equiv49}];


(* ::Section:: *)
(*50. Inline (L857, L861-862, L871-875): P + d_r psi = -g/r^2 for psi = g(u)/r; r psi constant along outgoing light rays, imposed as Theta psi; flat space: d_t(P + psi') = -P/r*)


(* LaTeX (L857): "$P+\partial_r\psi=-g(u)/r^2$ for a scalar wave $\psi=g(u)/r$"; (L861-862) "$r\psi=g(u)$ must be constant along
   the outgoing characteristics, of speed ... $1$"; (L871-872) "For the scalar we impose that $\Theta\psi$ be constant along the
   outgoing light rays" + DATA "scalarRate" (L871-875); (L852, L803-805) the entering scalar field is P + d_r psi.
   Check (derivation): (u + e).grad(Theta psi), reduced with the kinematic definitions (P = u.grad psi, d_t Theta), equals
   Theta (P + psi' + c psi) with exactly the code's c; for the flat outgoing wave psi = g(t-r)/r (N = 1, beta = 0, Theta = r,
   Q = trK = 0) P + psi' + c psi = 0 identically, while the entering combination P + psi' = -g/r^2 is not zero (so the code
   prescribes its rate, d_t(P + psi') = -d_t(c psi)); (1, 1) is the left eigenvector of [[beta, N],[N, beta]] for beta + N.
   Flat space with P = d_t psi: X = P + psi' + psi/r = r^-1 (d_t + d_r)(r psi) and d_t X = d_t(P + psi') + P/r IDENTICALLY, so
   d_t(P + psi') = -P/r <=> d_t X = 0 <=> (d_t + d_r)(r psi) = 0 once X = 0 at r_max before the wave arrives (the equivalence
   is through the time derivative; for the spin-0 pair it is pointwise, S49); for psi = g(t-r)/r (a solution of the flat wave
   equation) P + psi' = -g/r^2 and d_t(P + psi') = -g'/r^2 = -P/r: the rate is that of the 1/r^2 part. *)
Block[{lhs, ps},
  lhs = kinReduce[(uUp + eUp) . Table[D[Thf[t, r] psi[t, r], X[[a]]], {a, 4}]];
  ps = gg[t - r]/r;
  res50 = {Simplify[lhs - Thf[t, r] (Pf[t, r] + D[psi[t, r], r] + (D[Thf[t, r], r]/Thf[t, r] + Qf[t, r]/2 - trk[t, r]/3) psi[t, r])],
     Simplify[D[ps, t] + D[ps, r] + (1/r) ps], Simplify[D[ps, t] + D[ps, r] + gg[t - r]/r^2],
     Simplify[{1, 1} . {{bt, nn}, {nn, bt}} - (bt + nn) {1, 1}],
     Simplify[(D[ps50[t, r], t] + D[ps50[t, r], r] + ps50[t, r]/r) - (D[r ps50[t, r], t] + D[r ps50[t, r], r])/r],
     Simplify[D[D[ps50[t, r], t] + D[ps50[t, r], r] + ps50[t, r]/r, t] - (D[D[ps50[t, r], t] + D[ps50[t, r], r], t] + D[ps50[t, r], t]/r)],
     Simplify[D[ps, {t, 2}] - D[r^2 D[ps, r], r]/r^2],
     Simplify[D[D[ps, t] + D[ps, r], t] + D[ps, t]/r]};
];
report["S50 scalar boundary datum", "803-805,852,857,861-862," <> datL["scalarRate"] <> ",collapse.cpp:L917-928", "(u+e)(Theta psi) = Theta (P + psi' + c psi), c = Theta'/Theta + Q/2 - trK/3 = the code's c; exact for g(t-r)/r; entering field P + psi' = -g/r^2; flat: d_t X = d_t(P + psi') + P/r with X = r^-1 (d_t + d_r)(r psi), so d_t(P + psi') = -P/r <=> (d_t + d_r)(r psi) = 0 given X = 0 initially; g(t-r)/r obeys it", isZeroAll[res50], res50];


(* ::Section:: *)
(*51. The scalar condition as implemented in the code (through d_t P alone)*)


(* LaTeX (L851-853, L871-872): the entering scalar field P + d_r psi changes as for an outgoing wave; "the outgoing fields simply
   leave".  (The paper does not describe the projection, "keep the outgoing part unchanged and replace the entering part";
   this section is a check of the code.)
   Check (derivation): for the pair (P, phi) with M = [[beta, N],[N, beta]]: entering theta = (1, 1), e = (1, 1)/2; the
   projector update is d_t u = P R + e B.  Both give d_t(P + phi) = B (the entering condition is the same).  For the outgoing
   combination P - phi the projector gives R_P - R_phi (unchanged), the code B - 2 R_phi: they differ by
   B - R_P - R_phi = -(theta.R - B), which vanishes only when the interior equations already give the outgoing-wave rate.
   The paper does not describe this detail; the check shows that it is equivalent for outgoing waves.  PASS: the difference is
   -(theta.R - B), which vanishes for an outgoing wave (B = R_P + R_phi); for the spin-0 pair the update is exact (S48). *)
Block[{Rv, ein, th, Pm, proj, code},
  Rv = {RP, Rphi}; th = {1, 1}; ein = {1, 1}/2; Pm = IdentityMatrix[2] - Outer[Times, ein, th];
  proj = Pm . Rv + ein Bs; code = {Bs - Rphi, Rphi};
  res51 = Simplify[{th . proj - Bs, th . code - Bs, {1, -1} . proj - (RP - Rphi), {1, -1} . (code - proj) + (th . Rv - Bs)}];
  code51 = code; proj51 = proj;
];
report["S51 scalar pair in the code", datL["outgoingUnchanged"] <> ",collapse.cpp:L917-928", "code imposes d_t(P+psi') = B through d_t P alone: same entering condition; d_t(P-psi') differs from the projector form by -(theta_in.R - B), zero for outgoing waves (B = R_P + R_psi'): the outgoing scalar equation is unchanged for outgoing waves (code check)",
  isZeroAll[res51] && Simplify[({1, -1} . (code51 - proj51)) /. Bs -> RP + Rphi] === 0, res51];


(* ::Section:: *)
(*52. Outflow gate of the code: beta < -v0 N (spin-0) and beta < -N (scalar) (not described in the paper; code check)*)


(* LaTeX: none (the paper does not describe the outflow gate); the paper's statement that a condition is
   needed only for the entering fields (L851-853) and the code gate remain.
   Check (derivation): with N, v0 > 0, beta + N v0 < 0 && beta - N v0 < 0  <=>  beta < -v0 N, and likewise with v0 -> 1
   for the scalar pair (eigenvalues beta +- N, S41); the code's gate (collapse.cpp:L1001-1030, s0/sc at L1012) switches the
   condition on iff bt + N v0 > 0 (resp. bt + N > 0), bt = beta + R_t the shift relative to the grid (printed as NRm in the
   code's log lines). *)
res52 = {Reduce[ForAll[{bt, nn, v0}, nn > 0 && v0 > 0, Equivalent[bt + nn v0 < 0 && bt - nn v0 < 0, bt < -v0 nn]], Reals],
   Reduce[ForAll[{bt, nn}, nn > 0, Equivalent[bt + nn < 0 && bt - nn < 0, bt < -nn]], Reals]};
report["S52 outflow gate (code)", "collapse.cpp:L1001-1030", "both eigenvalues negative <=> beta < -v0 N (spin-0), beta < -N (scalar)", res52 === {True, True}, res52];


(* ::Section:: *)
(*53. Inline (L857-860, L877-882): setting w_in to zero reflects by the ratio of the falloffs, ~ pulse width/r_max; 3.5% and 2.3%*)


(* LaTeX (L857-860): "Setting these fields to zero at $r_{\max}$, their value at infinity, therefore reflects part of the wave,
   by the ratio of the two falloffs, i.e.\ about the pulse width over $r_{\max}$."  (L877-881) "A spin-0 pulse $\trK\propto\exp[-(r-50)^2/16]$ crossing a flat-space boundary at
   $r_{\max}=100$ and $150$, for $v_0=1$ and $1.267$, is reflected into $\win$ below $10^{-5}$ of the incident $\wout$, against
   $3.5\%$ ($r_{\max}=100$) and $2.3\%$ ($r_{\max}=150$) when $\win$ is set to zero."  (3.48% x 100/150 = 2.32%: the 1/r_max
   scaling of the falloff ratio.)
   Check (derivation): data trK = g(r) = exp[-(r-50)^2/16], a_r = 0 at t = 0.  The exact linear solution is
   r trK = [G(r - v0 t) + G(r + v0 t)]/2 with G(s) = s g(s); the outgoing part has f(u) = G(-v0 u)/2 and, ahead of it,
   a_r = 0 fixes the static Coulomb term to zero, so at r_max w_in = -bN F(u)/r_max^2 rises from 0 to -bN F_inf/r_max^2 with
   F_inf = Int G ds/(2 v0), while w_out = -(bN/v0)[G/r + Fhat/r^2] (Fhat(s) = Int_s^inf G/2).  Freezing w_in (B = 0) leaves a
   reflected entering field of amplitude |bN| F_inf/r_max^2; relative to max|w_out| at r_max this is
   Fhat(0)/r_max^2 / max_s[G(s)/r_max + Fhat(s)/r_max^2], independent of v0 and bN: 3.48% (r_max = 100) and 2.33% (r_max = 150),
   i.e. ~ (sqrt(pi) x 4/2) x (G peak ~ r0) ... / r_max: of relative size width/r_max as stated.  Both printed values match. *)
Block[{Gs, Fh, finf, ratio},
  Gs[s_] := s Exp[-(s - 50)^2/16];
  Fh[s_] = Integrate[x Exp[-(x - 50)^2/16]/2, {x, s, Infinity}, Assumptions -> s \[Element] Reals];
  finf = N[Fh[0], 20];
  ratio[R_] := (finf/R^2)/First[FindMaximum[Gs[s]/R + Fh[s]/R^2, {s, 50}, WorkingPrecision -> 20]];
  refl53 = N[{ratio[100], ratio[150]}];
];
(* release/VALIDATION.md (release/analysis/boundary_reflection.py): spin-0 reflection with the shipped code 5.6e-7, 4.1e-7
   (v0 = 1, R = 100, 150), 1.5e-6, 7.5e-7 (v0 = 1.267); pre-fix code 3.45/2.33 % and 3.53/2.33 %; scalar 2.8e-4 *)
val53 = {{5.6*^-7, 4.1*^-7, 1.5*^-6, 7.5*^-7}, {{3.45, 2.33}, {3.53, 2.33}}, 2.8*^-4};
ok53 = close[100 refl53[[1]], dat["reflSpin0"][[6]], 0.05] && close[100 refl53[[2]], dat["reflSpin0"][[7]], 0.05] &&
   Max[val53[[1]]] < dat["reflSpin0"][[5]] && And @@ (closeAll[#, {dat["reflSpin0"][[6]], dat["reflSpin0"][[7]]}, 0.05 + 10^-9] & /@ val53[[2]]) &&
   close[100 val53[[3]], dat["reflScalar"][[1]], 0.005 + 10^-9];
report["S53 w_in set to zero: reflection", "857-860,877-882", "linear theory of the paper's pulse gives " <> ToString[NumberForm[100 refl53[[1]], 3]] <> "% (r_max=100, printed 3.5%) and " <> ToString[NumberForm[100 refl53[[2]], 3]] <> "% (r_max=150, printed 2.3%); ~ width/r_max as stated; release record: spin-0 <= 1.5e-6 < 1e-5, pre-fix 3.45-3.53% / 2.33%, scalar 2.8e-4 -> 0.03%",
  ok53, 100 refl53];


