(*67. Inline (L1121-1124): the linear Coulomb term cancels up to O(M/Theta); -3/4 c13 Q^2   [DATA["coulombClaim"], DATA["q2Claim"]]*)


(* LaTeX (L1121-1124): "Integrating Eq.~\eqref{eq:dm-coulomb} inward from a sphere not yet reached by the wave shows that, up to
   $O(M/\Theta)$ corrections, $E$ is the integral of the quadratic and higher-order field energy outside $\Theta$ ... this
   quadratic energy density is not positive definite, due to shear contributions from the \ae ther stress tensor, yielding
   $-\tfrac{3}{4}c_{13}Q^2$, which is negative for $c_{13}>0$."
   Check (derivation, from S61): d_Theta m_c = d_Theta m - (c14/2) d_Theta(Theta^2 a) = (c14/2)(Theta'-1) d_Theta(Theta^2 a)
   + quadratic.  On the black-hole background Theta' = sqrt(1-2M/Theta) = 1 - M/Theta + ..., so the linear term fails to
   cancel at order Theta^-1: the claimed order (DATA["coulombClaim"] = 1) must equal the derived one.  The Q^2 coefficient of
   rho_ae (S59) must be the quoted -3/4 c13 (DATA["q2Claim"]), in the kappa = 1 normalisation. *)
